    "article_summary": "The article describes the first example of visible-light-driven acceptorless photodehydrogenation of benzylic alcohols to carboxylic acids using a single ruthenium(II) N-heterocyclic carbene (NHC) complex. The catalyst, complex I, serves a dual role as both a photosensitizer and a catalytic center, enabling the reaction in aqueous media at room temperature without external oxidants, producing H2 as the only byproduct.",
